  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Siemens Medical Solutions Usa reported $234M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Siemens Medical Solutions Usa won 491 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $477K. Siemens Medical Solutions Usa obligations are up 43.6% year over year. Siemens Medical Solutions Usa has seen variability in annual obligations: FY21 was $184M, FY22 was $223M, FY23 was $226M, FY24 was $231M, and FY25 was $163M. Siemens Medical Solutions Usa received its largest share of FY2026 obligations from the Department of Veterans Affairs, which obligated $195M. Siemens Medical Solutions Usa recorded $226M in the Irradiation Apparatus Manufacturing market, with smaller totals in related NAICS categories including Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance at $6M and Electromedical and Electrotherapeutic Apparatus Manufacturing at $448K. These figures are fiscal year to date and reflect contract obligations unless noted as total contract values in award tables.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Siemens Medical Solutions Usa's federal business trended recently?",
        "body": "Siemens Medical Solutions Usa obligations increased to $234M in FY2026 to date, up 43.6% year over year. Siemens Medical Solutions Usa yearly obligations moved from $184M in FY21 to $223M in FY22, $226M in FY23, $231M in FY24, and $163M in FY25. Siemens Medical Solutions Usa shows a rebound in FY2026 relative to FY25."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the main buyers and what markets drive Siemens Medical Solutions Usa federal sales?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer for Siemens Medical Solutions Usa at $195M, followed by the Department of Defense at $37M and the Department of Health and Human Services at $2.4M. The Irradiation Apparatus Manufacturing market drives most of Siemens Medical Solutions Usa obligations at $226M, with Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance at $6M and Electromedical and Electrotherapeutic Apparatus Manufacturing at $448K."
      }
    ]
  },
